5,Yuracare Language and the Yuracare Indian Tribe (Yura),https://www.native-languages.org/yuracare.htm,"Yuracare language information and the culture, history and genealogy of the Yuracare Indians.",Yuracare,Language isolate
6,"Yuracare Language (YUZ) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map, Endangered Level & Official Use | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/yuz/,Yuracare is an endangered indigenous language of Bolivia. It is an isolate that is not known to be related to any other language. The language is used as a first language by adults only. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Yuracare,Language isolate
7,Yuracare Language and the Yuracare Indian Tribe (Yura),http://www.native-languages.org/yuracare.htm,"Language: Yuracare, also known as Yura, is a South American language isolate, spoken by 2000 people in central Bolivia.",Yuracare,Language isolate
8,Yurakaré - Language,https://dobes.mpi.nl/projects/yurakare/language/,"January 9, 2014 - The Yurakaré language is spoken by the people of the same name (also Yuracaré, Yurucare, Yurujure) who form a small indigenous group that lives in the foothill area of the Andes in central Bolivia (see Geography). There are no reliable … Continue Reading →",Yuracare,Language isolate
9,Yuracare in Bolivia people group profile | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/16074/BL,"The Yuracare people are an indigenous group native to central Bolivia, primarily residing along the Chapare, Ichilo, and Sécure rivers in the departments of Cochabamba and Beni. Their language, Yuracare (also called Yurújare), is a language isolate, meaning it is not known to be related to any other language family.",Yuracare,Language isolate
